<!--
	Roaming fake players (see config/Custom/FakePlayerPvp.ini).

	kit: gear worn by a fake player. Each tier is used from its minLevel until the next tier
	     (1 = no grade, 20 = D, 40 = C, 52 = B, 61 = A, 76 = S, 80 = S80, 84 = S84).
	     Stats are read from the item data, so any item id can be used.

	buffs: buffs a fake player keeps on itself, like a player coming from the buffer.
	     Tiers add up: a level 76 fighter gets the 1, 40, 61 and 76 lists. Format: id,level;id,level
	     Buffs sharing an abnormal type (e.g. Chant of Victory, Magnus' Chant and the Prophecies,
	     or Greater Might and Greater Shield) overwrite each other, so list only one of them.

	build: a class a fake player can be.
	     classId - the final (3rd) class; below 76 the matching 2nd/1st/base class is used.
	     role    - FIGHTER, TANK, DAGGER (melee), ARCHER (keeps distance) or MAGE (casts and kites).
	     buffs   - buff list to use, default MAGE for mystic classes and FIGHTER for the others.
	     weight  - relative chance to pick this build.
	     Skills are lists of skill ids. The level of each skill (and whether the fake player
	     has it at all) comes from the class skill tree for its level, like a real character.
	     "a|b|c" means only the first learned one is used (e.g. exclusive totems).
	     attack    - damage skills, most preferred first.
	     debuff    - stuns, roots and debuffs (mostly used against players).
	     buff      - self buffs kept up while fighting.
	     heal      - self heals.
	     emergency - used below 30% HP.
	     toggle    - toggles switched on at spawn.
	     Class passive skills (masteries, etc.) for the level are always added.
-->
